module coroutine.sus

--[[
`coroutine.sus` connects readiness sources to suspension handlers.
Use [](coroutine.suspend) to wait for a value from a callback.

```nupp:fragment
local suspension = coroutine.sus

local function readLine(reader: Reader): string
    return coroutine.suspend("example.readLine", function(
        resume: function(string),
        context: suspension.Context
    ): function()
        const subscription = reader:onLine(resume)

        return function(): nil
            subscription:release()
        end
    end)
end
```

[](coroutine.suspend) waits for a value, `source` registers the pump that makes
it ready, and `poll` drives every registered pump once.
`handled` says whether a handler is listening; without one a park drives those
pumps on this thread and blocks after all. `cansuspend` returns whether a park
would be permitted here at all, and `create` makes a coroutine that inherits the
handler.

Installing a handler, and driving the parks it accepts, is the other side of
this: [](coroutine.sus.host). A library needs none of it.

This is the layer underneath. Somewhere to put children discovered over time,
with one answer for failure and cancellation, is [](coroutine); real
parallelism is [](coroutine.workers). Come here directly to make a library waitable,
or to write a combinator neither of those has.

An arbitrary blocking Lua or C call still blocks the thread. A library opts in
by calling [](coroutine.suspend); nothing intercepts calls that do not.

See [suspension.md](docs/learn/runtime/concurrency/suspension.md).
]]
local contract = require("nupp.suspension.spi")
local source1 = require("nupp.suspension")
export type Context = source1.Context
export type Source = source1.Source
export const Context = source1.Context
export const Source = source1.Source
export const cansuspend: contract.Provider.["cansuspend"] = source1.canSuspend
export const create: contract.Provider.["create"] = source1.create
export const handled: contract.Provider.["handled"] = source1.handled
export const poll: contract.Provider.["poll"] = source1.poll
export const source: contract.Provider.["source"] = source1.source
